{
  "id": "konjugation",
  "name": "Key irregular verbs in the present",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "es419": { "note": "In Latin America the vosotros forms (sois, vais, tenéis) are not used. Ustedes takes the ellos form: son, van, tienen." },
  "subtitle": "The most useful Spanish verbs do not follow the rules: ser, estar, ir, tener, hacer, venir. Some are irregular only in the yo form: salgo, pongo, conozco.",
  "briefMarks": ["ser", "estar", "ir", "tener", "hacer", "venir"],
  "lookup": { "href": "/present-simple", "label": "Regular verbs first? Present tense: -ar, -er, -ir" },
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "yo", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "soy · estoy · voy · tengo · hago · vengo", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-verb\">Soy</span> de Senegal. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Estoy</span> en casa. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Voy</span> al trabajo. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Tengo</span> dos hijos. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Hago</span> la compra.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>ser, estar, ir</strong> are irregular in almost every person. Learn them whole: <em>soy, eres, es…</em> / <em>estoy, estás, está…</em> / <em>voy, vas, va…</em>",
        "tag": "Learn them whole"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>tener</strong> and <strong>venir</strong> have <em>-go</em> in the yo form and a vowel change in other persons: <em>tengo, tienes, tiene, tenemos, tenéis, tienen</em>; <em>vengo, vienes, viene, venimos, venís, vienen</em>.",
        "tag": "tener, venir"
      },
      {
        "html": "Some verbs are irregular <strong>only in the yo form</strong>. After that they are regular: <em>hacer → hago, haces…; poner → pongo, pones…; salir → salgo, sales…; conocer → conozco, conoces…; saber → sé, sabes…; ver → veo, ves…; dar → doy, das…</em>",
        "tag": "Only yo"
      },
      {
        "html": "Spanish uses <strong>tener</strong> where English uses “be”: <em>Tengo 30 años. Tengo hambre. Tengo frío.</em> Not: <em>Soy 30 años.</em>",
        "tag": "tener for age"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>ir a</strong> says where you go: <em>Voy a Madrid. Vamos al médico.</em> <strong>venir de</strong> says where you come from: <em>Vengo del trabajo.</em>",
        "tag": "ir a, venir de"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Soy 25 años</em> → ✓ <em>Tengo 25 años</em>. ✗ <em>Yo teno</em> → ✓ <em>Yo tengo</em>. ✗ <em>Yo sabo</em> → ✓ <em>Yo sé</em>. ✗ <em>Vo a casa</em> → ✓ <em>Voy a casa</em>. When to use ser or estar: <a href=\"/word-order\">ser and estar</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "The six key verbs",
          "head": ["", "ser", "estar", "ir", "tener", "hacer", "venir"],
          "rows": [
            ["yo", "soy", "estoy", "voy", "tengo", "hago", "vengo"],
            ["tú", "eres", "estás", "vas", "tienes", "haces", "vienes"],
